:name: nRF52840 DK
:description: The nRF52840 DK's sw0 and led0, for Twister and renode-nrf-run.
:
: Both runners set $elf before including this file and start the emulation themselves,
: so there is no `start` here. renode-nrf-run finds it as boards/<board>.resc, Twister
: through `resc:` in the variant's yaml.
:
: Renode also ships platforms/boards/nrf52840dk_nrf52840.repl, and it is not used here.
: Its buttons have no `invert: true`, so pin 11 reads low at rest. The DK's buttons are
: active low, which makes the firmware see sw0 as held down from boot, and a press is
: only noticed when it is released. The button and LED below are wired the way the DK is.

set platform
"""
using "platforms/cpus/nrf52840.repl"

gpio0:
    13 -> led0@0

led0: Miscellaneous.LED @ gpio0 13
    invert: true

sw0: Miscellaneous.Button @ gpio0 11
    invert: true
    -> gpio0@11
"""

using sysbus
mach create "nrf52840dk"
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString $platform


macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $elf
"""
runMacro $reset
